Third-party material

nghttp2 (MIT) and cJSON (MIT) are not vendored: nghttp2 comes from the espressif/nghttp managed component and cJSON from
ESP-IDF's json component, both fetched at build time.

The tunnel protocol (edge TLS name, HTTP/2 stream conventions, Cap'n Proto registration schema, remote configuration
format) was implemented from the public cloudflared sources (https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared, Apache-2.0).
No cloudflared code is copied.

cf_edge_roots.c contains the public Cloudflare edge CA certificates taken from cloudflared's tlsconfig/cloudflare_ca.go
(Apache-2.0). They are public trust anchors.
